## Page Name: Dashboard
# Page Requirements:
Display a personalized greeting and learning status.
Show key learning metrics and progress summaries.
Provide quick access to continue learning or explore courses.
Present recent activity and achievements.
Offer insights into daily goals, learning streaks, and XP earned.
Include visual analytics for weekly and monthly activity.
Display a leaderboard to compare performance with peers.
Provide AI-driven course recommendations.
Allow users to view and track their learning progress across multiple subjects.
Support navigation to other sections of the platform.
Page Functionalities:
Personalized user greeting and learning status message.
Quick action buttons: "Continue Learning" and "View All Courses".
Display of key metrics: courses learned, lessons completed, problems solved, streak days, XP earned, and total rank.
"Continue Learning" section with in-progress course details and progress percentage.
Learning progress tracking for multiple subjects (e.g., Python, Java, C++).
Daily goal tracking with completion status (e.g., solve 5 problems, complete 1 quiz).
Activity calendar showing daily engagement over the past year.
Weekly analytics chart displaying time spent, XP gained, and problems solved.
Leaderboard showing top users and the current user’s rank.
Recent activity log listing completed tasks, earned XP, and milestones.
Achievements section with badges for milestones (e.g., 7-day streak, first certificate).
AI recommendation system suggesting next learning steps.
Navigation sidebar linking to Courses, Practice, Community, Profile, and Settings.
Integration with calendar apps for scheduling learning sessions.
Logout functionality.






## Page Name: Courses

### Page Requirements:
Display a list of all available courses with relevant metadata.
Allow users to view and manage their enrolled courses.
Enable filtering and sorting of courses based on various criteria.
Provide course progress tracking for enrolled users.
Offer recommendations based on user interests or learning history.
Support search functionality to find specific courses.
Allow users to continue learning from where they left off.
Display course ratings, difficulty levels, and completion status.
Show course categories and tags for better organization.
Provide access to course details and enrollment options.
Page Functionalities:
"My Courses" section showing currently enrolled courses with progress indicators.
"All Courses" section displaying a grid of available courses with thumbnails, titles, and metadata.
Search bar to find courses by name or topic.
Filter options by category (e.g., Programming, Web Development, AI, Cyber Security), difficulty (Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced), and status (Completed).
Sort options: Favorites, Newest, Most Popular.
Course cards showing title, instructor, rating, duration, lessons, and progress percentage.
"Continue Learning" button to resume progress in enrolled courses.
"Resume Python" button for quick access to in-progress courses.
"Recommended for You" section with personalized course suggestions.
Course difficulty labels (Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced).
Course tags (e.g., Python, JavaScript, React, Docker, Kubernetes).
Progress bars indicating completion percentage for each course.
Navigation to course details or enrollment page.
Responsive grid layout for course display.



